.TH GITEA-CREATE-OWNER.SH 1 "2026-04-28" "GitMirror" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gitea-create-owner.sh \- create a user account or organisation on a Gitea instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash gitea-create-owner.sh
.RB [ \-o ]
.I name
.RI [ password ]
.RI [ email ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gitea-create-owner.sh
creates a new user account or organisation on a Gitea instance.
.PP
If the user or organisation name is already taken, the script exits with an error and does not attempt to recreate it.
.PP
Without
.BR \-o ,
a user account is created. A password is required and will be prompted interactively if not supplied as a positional argument. The email address defaults to
.I name@users.noreply.github.com
when not provided.
.PP
Passwords for user creation must be at least 8 characters.
.PP
With
.BR \-o ,
an organisation is created. No password or email is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o
Create an organisation instead of a user account.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I name
Username or organisation name to create.
.TP
.I password
Password for the new user account. Prompted securely if omitted. Not used when
.B \-o
is set. Must be at least 8 characters.
.TP
.I email
Email address for the new user account. Defaults to
.IR name @users.noreply.github.com .
Not used when
.B \-o
is set.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B GITEA_URL
Base URL of the Gitea instance.
.TP
.B GITEA_TOKEN
Gitea API token. Creating a user account requires an admin-level token.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success. Returns 1 if the user or organisation already exists. Returns 2 for invalid usage, missing prerequisites, or missing configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a user account, prompting for password:
.PP
.B bash gitea-create-owner.sh alice
.PP
Create a user account with password and custom email:
.PP
.B bash gitea-create-owner.sh alice s3cr3t alice@example.com
.PP
Create an organisation:
.PP
.B bash gitea-create-owner.sh \-o my-org
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-mirror.sh (1),
.BR gitea-sync-all.sh (1)
